      <description>&lt;p&gt;क्षिप꣡ ॐ꣡ स्वा꣡हा!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;कुङ्कुमाङ्कित-वर्णाय&lt;br&gt;&#xA;कुन्देन्दु धवलाय च।&lt;br&gt;&#xA;विष्णु-वाह नमस् तुभ्यं&lt;br&gt;&#xA;पक्षिराजाय ते नमः॥&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>गरुडदण्डकम्</title>
      <link>https://vishvAsa.github.io/devaH/AryaH/hindukaH/garuDaH/padyam/garuDa-daNDakam/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://vishvAsa.github.io/devaH/AryaH/hindukaH/garuDaH/padyam/garuDa-daNDakam/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;js_include&#34; includetitle=&#34;true&#34; newlevelforh1=&#34;2&#34; unfilled url=&#34;https://vishvAsa.github.io/devaH/purANam_vaiShNavam/kAvyam/padyam/shrIvaiShNava-kRtam/venkaTanAthaH/garuDa-daNDakam/&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;details open&gt;&lt;summary&gt;&lt;h2&gt;गरुडदण्डकम् ...{Loading}...&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt;गानानि&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;&lt;div caption=&#34;भार्गवी, श्रीमती&#34; class=&#34;videoEmbed&#34; src=&#34;https://youtu.be/fxseucTKDaU?si=NHvTDwaEWlOFZNto&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div caption=&#34;दुष्यन्तः&#34; class=&#34;videoEmbed&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=djsWS1UTD-w&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt;शठकोपः (En)&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.sadagopan.org/ebook/pdf/Garuda%20Dhandakam.pdf&#34;&gt;TW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In sanskrit poetry, each of the 4 Paadas of a sloka can have 26 letters. If the letters of each Paadas increase to 27,30,33,36 (other multiples of 3 beyond 27), then this slokam is recognized as a Dhandakam. The 3 lettered units are known as a GaNa. Thus a 27 lettered Paada will have 9 GaNaas.There is generally no restriction on the length of the Paada in a Dhandakam.Swami Desikan chose Paadas with 36 GaNaas or 108 = (32X4) letters for the four Paadas of Garuda Dhandakam. The poetic genius of Swami Desikan is abundantly evident in this Composition. The Paadas of this Dhandakam parsed by its 144 GaNaas make intricate swoops in the air and make sharp turns like the high soaring Pakshi Raja (Garuda).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
